        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds missing support data for <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;meta name=\"viewport\"&gt;</code>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR assumes that Mobile Safari 3 for iOS shipped the first <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;meta name=\"viewport\"&gt;</code> implementation, and all later released mobile browsers followed.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://blog.mozilla.org/en/mozilla/mozilla-launches-firefox-4-for-android-allowing-users-to-take-the-power-and-customization-of-firefox-everywhere-2/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Firefox 4 for Android</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://chromereleases.googleblog.com/2012/06/chrome-for-android-out-of-beta.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chrome 18 for Android</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20110920142131/http://www.opera.com/docs/specs/productspecs/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Opera Mobile 10</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There’s a <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/7929/designing-websites-for-iphone-x/\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">viewport-fit</code> feature</a> that Safari 11 presumably shipped. I just learned that Chrome is planning to ship it soon, too.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #25311.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2715504565\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25311\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25311/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25311\">#25311</a></p>",
